  <!-- Systemic Gap Section -->
<section class="gap-section redesigned-gap">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gap-header">
      <div class="section-icon">
        <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <path d="M12 2L13.09 8.26L20 9L13.09 9.74L12 16L10.91 9.74L4 9L10.91 8.26L12 2Z" fill="currentColor"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Why is there such a systemic technology gap in the social sector?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="gap-content">
      <div class="gap-paragraph">
        <span class="highlight-quote">When the world's biggest servers hum to open-source code,</span>
        <p>it's ironic non-profits still run on Google Sheets.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gap-paragraph">
        <p>Experiments had already started in 2021 by <strong>FOSS United</strong>, <strong>Tech4Good community</strong>, <strong>Reap Benefit</strong>, <strong>Aikyam Fellows</strong> and <strong>TinkerHub</strong> in the form of tech volunteering, some software development, partnering with various NGOs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gap-paragraph">
        <p>What began as scattered experiments and caffeine-fueled conversations, slowly drew a circle of like-minded tinkers, people trying in their own corners, to gather at the <strong>Zerodha office, J.P. Nagar</strong> one fine day. They decided to build meaningful tech muscle for the social sector.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gap-paragraph">
        <p>While unpacking social sector roadblocks <em>one filter coffee at a time</em>, we realised the fixes couldn't come from quick hacks. Addressing these challenges requires a multi-faceted approach, one that turns digital potential from a 'good-to-have' into an absolute essential.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gap-paragraph highlight-end">
        <p>Soon after, the group was formalized as an alliance, <strong>OASIS (Open-source Alliance for Social Innovation and Sustainability)</strong>.</p>
        <div class="oasis-logo">
          <svg width="80" height="80" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M12 2L13.09 8.26L20 9L13.09 9.74L12 16L10.91 9.74L4 9L10.91 8.26L12 2Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
            <text x="12" y="14" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">OASIS</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

